# The TERM of the tmux client that create_popup_session attaches inside a
# popup. tmux treats a terminal as VT100-like when clear starts with CSI and
# then sends it queries (DA, OSC 10/11, CSI 14t) that a popup never fully
# answers; while one is open, tmux holds a lone Escape for 500 ms whatever
# escape-time says. The cursor save/restore in front of the usual clear makes
# tmux skip the queries; tmux.conf names the features they would have found.
tmux-popup|tmux client inside a tmux popup,
	clear=\E7\E8\E[H\E[J, use=tmux-256color,
